# Line endings.
#
# Every blob in this repository is already stored with LF — the only thing that
# was ever CRLF was the working tree on a Windows machine with
# `core.autocrlf=true`. That mismatch made `npm run format:check` report all 161
# files as unformatted, because Prettier's `endOfLine` default is "lf". A
# documented pre-launch step (see DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md) was therefore permanently
# red and carried no signal.
#
# `eol=lf` takes precedence over each developer's `core.autocrlf`, so the
# working tree is LF on every machine and Prettier's strict default passes on
# its own. The alternative — setting `endOfLine: "auto"` in .prettierrc.json —
# would have silenced the check rather than fixed it: Prettier would then accept
# whatever endings a file happened to have, and the repository could quietly
# acquire mixed endings with nothing left to catch it.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content and leave it alone; the
# explicit `-text` rules below make that guarantee obvious for the image assets
# rather than leaving it to detection.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  -text
*.webp -text
*.ico  -text
*.jpg  -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif  -text
*.pdf  -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text

# 3D and design source assets (design/ inbox for ATLAS mode).
*.glb   -text
*.gltf  -text
*.bin   -text
*.hdr   -text
*.exr   -text
*.ktx2  -text
*.fbx   -text
*.mp4   -text
*.webm  -text
